Canonical Principle

Culture, theology, mythology, and healthcare all shape how people understand identity and authority, but they cannot be governed as one undifferentiated domain.

The governing boundaries are:

interpretation is not empirical proof
public reference is not institutional endorsement
symbolic meaning is not legal authority
technical capability is not clinical authorization
identity representation is not medical judgment
documentation is not activation readiness

The repository must preserve human dignity, plural interpretation, institutional accuracy, professional boundaries, and traceable authority across every use.